# Telegram Control

Control vPilot from your Telegram bot, and get connect/broadcast notices there.
Private messages, radio, SELCAL, disconnect and Hoppie relaying are already handled by
VBuddy's normal notifier; this feature adds the **two-way** part.

## Setup

1. Create a bot and get your `BotToken` and `ChatId` (see [telegram.md](telegram.md)).
2. Add to `VBuddy.ini`:

```ini
[Telegram]
BotToken="123456:ABC-your-token"
ChatId="123456789"

[TelegramControl]
Enabled=true
RelayBroadcast=true
NotifyConnect=true
NotifyDisconnect=false
```

`[TelegramControl]` reuses the `[Telegram]` credentials. You can override them by adding
`BotToken` / `ChatId` under `[TelegramControl]` (e.g. to use a separate bot).

3. Restart vPilot. You should get "VBuddy Telegram control is online."

## Commands

| Command | Action |
| --- | --- |
| `/status` | Shows whether you're connected, and as which callsign |
| `/connect` | Connects using the last callsign / aircraft / SELCAL used in vPilot |
| `/connect CALLSIGN TYPECODE [SELCAL]` | Connects with explicit details |
| `/disconnect` | Disconnects from the network |
| `/msg CALLSIGN text` | Sends a private message |
| `/help` | Lists commands |

## Settings

| Key | Default | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `Enabled` | `false` | Master switch |
| `RelayBroadcast` | `true` | Forward network broadcast messages |
| `NotifyConnect` | `true` | Send a message when you connect |
| `NotifyDisconnect` | `false` | Send a message when you disconnect (leave off if `[Disconnect]` already does this) |

## Security

- Commands are only accepted from the configured `ChatId`. Anyone else messaging the bot is ignored silently.
- Treat the bot token like a password. If it leaks, revoke it in @BotFather with `/revoke`.
- Commands queued while vPilot was closed are discarded at startup, so an old `/disconnect` can't fire later.

## Notes

- Telegram allows only one program to poll a bot at a time. If another app (or a webhook)
  uses the same bot you'll see a "409" message in the vPilot debug window; use a dedicated bot.
- Your identity is remembered in `VBuddy.identity` next to `VBuddy.dll`.
